From: Qore Technologies <david@qore.org>
Subject: Apply inline visibility only to C++ compilation

Copyright 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

GYP's cflags apply to C and C++. V8 includes C sources, but GCC accepts
-fvisibility-inlines-hidden only for C++. Keep the shared-library visibility
policy and move its C++ component to the language-specific list.

--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
@@ -69,6 +69,8 @@
       }, '(OS!="aix" and OS!="os400") and (OS!="win" or clang==1)', {
         'cflags': [
           '-fvisibility=hidden',
+        ],
+        'cflags_cc': [
           '-fvisibility-inlines-hidden'
         ],
       }],  # MSVC hides the non-public symbols by default so no need to configure it.
